KCometen6 ChangeLog
===================

Version 1.0.2
  * Added a "Make "Portable" button to the GUI Panel for installs that use PKGBUILD which will install KCometen6 system-wide, but that method does not create a portable folder that you can move to another machine.  Use build_and_deploy.sh to build only a portable folder with no install. Run stage_release.sh to create a new clean source tree.  Read the header of stage_release.sh for instructions.  If you do not change the version number, it will overwrite ther last new source tree that you created. It's set for "kcometen6_v1.0.3" now.

  * Fixed the GUI Panel to allow spaces in names when creating or using portable folders.

  * Made the GUI Panel run directory aware so it now knows if it's running from a system-wide install or a portable folder in the home directory.
    A system-wide install parses settings.conf from /usr/share/kcometen6/.
    A portable folder parses settings.conf from ~/.config/kcometen6/.

  * Added system-path awareness to kcometen6_idle (Screensaver Mode).
    It will now dynamically use the system-wide kcometen6_run binary when installed in /usr/bin/, but falls back to the local kcometen6_run when started from a portable folder.

  * kcometen6_idle intercepts redundant execution requests, prints a protection log, and exits.

  * Dual-Aware Compilation Configuration (CMakeLists.txt)
    It targets nested src/ arrays for system-wide builds but falls back to loose folder files for your local programming tweaks.

  * Staging Automation (arch_release.sh)
    A custom release script, clearing out legacy compilation artifacts and splitting your loose development tree into structured layout folders (src/, textures/) inside a temporary staging buffer and creates a tarball in the root of your source tree without chaning your root tree (stage_release.sh & build_and_deploy.sh still work).

    Out-of-Source Package Installer (PKGBUILD)
  *  Modified the build() and package() blocks to compile out-of-source from your staging folder arrays, compile, inject custom desktop launcher profile strings, and map permissions system-wide.


Version 1.0.1
  * Port KCometen4 to KDE Plasma 6 & Wayland


KCometen4 ChangeLog
===================

Version 1.0.7
  * Work around a problem with Intel cards

Version 1.0.6
  * Explicitly link against libGL

Version 1.0.5
  * Spread out comet origination
  * Sync kcometen4.desktop translations with KDE 4.2.4
  * Remove resize hack; bug fixed in KDE 4.2.3
  * Clean up how the config changes interact with the preview
  * Small fixes to CMakeLists.txt files

Version 1.0.4
  * Change slow motion camera behavior
    - Slow motion effects have a selectable aspect ratio: 1.85:1, 2.40:1, and
      fullscreen.
    - Camera no longer always on the x-z plane
  * Possibly fix a bug that sometimes causes the background to appear black.
  * Update the CMakeLists files so it can build on Gentoo.

Version 1.0.3
  * Fix rendering of comet tails
    - Don't enable point smoothing.  It causes problems with some drivers.
    - If the driver doesn't support point sprites, use textured quads.
  * Reorganize the settings dialog and add a "Particle density" setting.

Version 1.0.2
  * Link to kio

Version 1.0.1
  * Fix compilation problems for some distributions.
  * Add a very basic configure script that wraps a few common cmake settings.
  * Add some notes to INSTALL.
  * Add a hack that stops the embedded OpenGL widget from resizing to 640x480.
    See KDE bug #165552.

Version 1.0
  * Port KCometen3 to KDE4
  * Plug a memory leak
  * Fix field of view distortions in very oblong windows
  * New options
    - set field of view (default: 76 degrees)
    - set whether scene dimensions should always be a cube (default: false)
    - use mipmaps (default: false)
  * Update the setup dialog
    - rearrange dialog and rename a few settings for clarity
    - add a dynamic preview
    - add About and Defaults buttons
    - add What's This? info
    - make it a KDialog
  * Improve the quality of the background image
    - add an option for 1024x1024 image size
    - use Qt::SmoothTransformation when scaling
